# AI Software Company Runtime V1.1 - real / proof model provider configuration
#
# This is an EXAMPLE ONLY. Copy it to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in a key, OR
# export these variables in your shell. NEVER put a real key in this file or in
# any file that is committed.
#
# The runtime does not read `.env` automatically; use `env $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs) ai-company ...`
# or simply `export` the variables. The API key is read from the *named* variable
# at call time and is never stored, logged, printed or written to the audit ledger.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PREFERRED V1.1 proof provider: Groq Direct
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# groq | openrouter | openai-compatible | disabled   (default: groq)
AI_COMPANY_REAL_PROVIDER=groq

# Base URL for the selected provider. Leave unset to use the provider default
# (Groq: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1).
# AI_COMPANY_REAL_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# Explicit model id override. Leave unset to use the provider default
# (Groq default: openai/gpt-oss-120b).
AI_COMPANY_REAL_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Optional tuning.
AI_COMPANY_REAL_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
AI_COMPANY_REAL_MAX_RETRIES=2

# Optional agent output-token controls (build spec section 7). Stages carry
# their own compact budgets; these override the runner default and the global
# safety ceiling. The runtime still detects OUTPUT_TRUNCATED and raises the
# budget once on a truncation retry.
# AI_COMPANY_AGENT_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=6000
# AI_COMPANY_AGENT_OUTPUT_TOKENS_CEILING=12000
#
# Rate-limit handling is automatic: the runtime learns Groq's per-window request
# and token budget from `x-ratelimit-*` / `Retry-After` response headers, paces
# real requests sequentially, and WAITS for the reset window on HTTP 429 (bounded
# retry cycles, then RATE_LIMIT_EXHAUSTED). Waiting for free-tier quota needs no
# Human Founder approval.

# The actual API key. Set this in your ENVIRONMENT ONLY - do not commit it.
# Groq Direct is a PROOF provider (NON_SENSITIVE_PROOF_ONLY); it is NOT an
# approved permanent production provider.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FREE-FIRST fallback proof provider: NVIDIA NIM (auto-engaged)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When NVIDIA_API_KEY is present, the Software Factory proof automatically falls
# back from Groq Direct to NVIDIA NIM if - and ONLY if - Groq reaches a bounded
# RATE_LIMIT_EXHAUSTED (its free-tier daily quota). The workflow checkpoint is
# preserved, only the blocked stage is retried, and completed stages / tool
# writes / artifacts are never repeated. NVIDIA NIM is also a PROOF provider
# (NON_SENSITIVE_PROOF_ONLY), never auto-selected for ordinary work, never paid.
#   provider id : nvidia
#   base URL    : https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
#   model       : nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
# Set NVIDIA as the PRIMARY instead with AI_COMPANY_REAL_PROVIDER=nvidia.
# Disable the auto fallback entirely with AI_COMPANY_REAL_FALLBACK=none.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL fallback proof provider: OpenRouter (still fully supported,
# but NEVER auto-added to the free-first fallback chain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To use OpenRouter instead, set:
#   AI_COMPANY_REAL_PROVIDER=openrouter
#   AI_COMPANY_REAL_MODEL=openrouter/free        # or a pinned model id
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<environment only>
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Advanced: point the generic OpenAI-compatible adapter at any other gateway.
#   AI_COMPANY_REAL_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
#   AI_COMPANY_REAL_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway/v1
#   AI_COMPANY_REAL_API_KEY_ENV=YOUR_KEY_VAR
#   YOUR_KEY_VAR=<environment only>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PREMIUM implementation escalation - implementation stage ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Off by default. Setting AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_PROVIDER IS the Human Founder
# authorization for ONE run: the `implementation` stage runs on the premium path,
# every other stage stays on the free-first chain, and the run is bounded to one
# primary attempt + one targeted repair. Any failure (bad code that fails a
# runtime gate, or a provider error) STOPS the run - no free fallback, no retry,
# no further spend. Never auto-engaged just because a free provider failed. Every
# deterministic gate stays authoritative; the premium output is never sufficient
# evidence of success; independent review stays intact.
#
# PREFERRED: the locally authenticated Codex CLI (ChatGPT login) - no paid API
# credit needed. Requires `codex login` (`codex login status` => "Logged in
# using ChatGPT"). OPENAI_API_KEY is stripped from the Codex child env.
#   AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_PROVIDER=codex-cli
#   AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_MODEL=              # optional; empty = account default
#
# ALTERNATIVE: the paid OpenAI Chat Completions API (needs org API credit).
#   AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_PROVIDER=openai
#   AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_MODEL=gpt-5.1       # default priority: gpt-5.1 -> gpt-5 -> gpt-4.1
#   AI_COMPANY_PREMIUM_IMPL_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
OPENAI_API_KEY=
